    {
      "id": "claim_ab68e81e3bfb4317b10a494db75a785e",
      "statement": "The entrypoint probes HOME by mkdir -p plus a -w test and falls back to a scratch /tmp/pi-home when the uid has no writable home, because git, npm and Pi all need somewhere to put state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://docker-entrypoint.sh#L5-L12",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2aeae3ad4346ad4782feb227a0342fe05b665f966fe0d8a9179ea242304a28df:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_adc828b820484978ac9218fbd734bba5",
      "statement": "Failure handling in the entrypoint is deliberate and split: the HOME probe and the git config call are tolerant, while the fallback mkdir is not and set -eu aborts the container if anything else fails.",
